WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(house band plays)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.860
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.952
Our next guest knows what
it's like to be surrounded

00:00:04.952 --> 00:00:05.940
by the extraordinary.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.520
Her dad, Clarence, known
as the Black Godfather,

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.030
was the chairman of Motown
Records, no big deal.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.730
Her mom, Jacqueline,
which, I love that name,

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.770
was a huge activist and philanthropist

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.690
in South Central Los Angeles.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.510
And, she's a powerhouse
in her own right, as well.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.030
Her new book is called
"Think You'll Be Happy,

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.970
Moving Through Grief With
Grit, Gratitude, and Grace."

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.010
Great title, great subject matter.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.024
Let's, everybody, welcome
back Nicole Avant. Come on!

00:00:32.024 --> 00:00:35.032
(audience cheers)

00:00:35.032 --> 00:00:36.570
So welcome, welcome back to the show.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.570
- Thank you.
- Yes.

00:00:38.577 --> 00:00:41.730
So, I have to ask, writing
a book is such a huge thing.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.680
Like, I don't know if I'd
ever do something like that.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.410
It's so hard, and it's,
you've gotta be so vulnerable,

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.303
and a lot has happened in your life.

00:00:48.303 --> 00:00:50.160
- Yes.
- Like, even since this is,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.470
you started the book,
and then throughout it.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.350
So, how do you deal, like,
the loss of your dad,

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.560
like, and going through
this book, and being honest.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.480
- You know, the writing helps,

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.130
as I'm sure a lot of
you guys know, writing,

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:02.963
and I'm sure you too.
- Oh man.

00:01:02.963 --> 00:01:05.986
- When you write it out for a song,

00:01:05.986 --> 00:01:08.310
it gets all of your emotions out.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.078
It helps you own what you're feeling.

00:01:10.078 --> 00:01:10.911
- And, I think.

00:01:10.911 --> 00:01:12.761
- It's almost like you
recognize what you are feeling.

00:01:12.761 --> 00:01:13.980
- You recognize what you're
feeling by writing it out.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.600
That's why journaling works. You know?

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.820
And, so yes, it was hard writing the book,

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.440
but it was hard in a good way.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.460
It was challenging.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.520
And, I had already been
writing a book, you know,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.730
before anything happened
with my mom and my dad.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.610
And, I had written it after
"The Black Godfather."

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.860
I thought the themes,
grit, gratitude, and grace,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.471
- Yeah.
Came out of the documentary,

00:01:34.471 --> 00:01:35.566
"The Black Godfather."
- Yeah.

00:01:35.566 --> 00:01:37.059
- And, that's what I was gonna write.

00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:38.070
And, then we actually
did, I was on the show.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.976
- Came on the show, I know.

00:01:39.976 --> 00:01:40.950
- And, you ended, and you
know, when you end a Zoom

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.470
and it says, "Leave now,"
we didn't actually leave.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.510
And, you said she should write a book.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.612
And, I was, just,

00:01:46.612 --> 00:01:49.711
I had just started "Grit,
Gratitude, and Grace."

00:01:49.711 --> 00:01:52.622
And, you were the one
who gave me the fuel.

00:01:52.622 --> 00:01:54.720
I kept saying, "I don't
know how to write this.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.984
I don't know what I'm doing,"
and you did that for me.

00:01:56.984 --> 00:01:58.851
(audience cheers)
So, you're a part.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.540
- 'Cause when you listen
to you speak about it,

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.400
you're such a great speaker
and you're so vulnerable.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.740
Not everybody's able to go to that place.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.573
- Yeah.

00:02:05.573 --> 00:02:07.050
- Like, that's a very hard place to go to.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.190
But, what I find interesting is,

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.390
so you were already writing,

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.187
You lose your mama, you lost your daddy.

00:02:11.187 --> 00:02:12.840
There's so much that happened,

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.225
and they weren't that far apart.

00:02:14.225 --> 00:02:15.058
- No.

00:02:15.058 --> 00:02:16.920
- Like, so much to happen
while you're writing this.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.531
So, it definitely had to alter the book.

00:02:18.531 --> 00:02:20.520
- It altered the book completely.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.517
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:21.517 --> 00:02:23.571
I, so, like I said, I was
starting on "Grits, Grace

00:02:23.571 --> 00:02:26.880
and Gratitude," and then my
mom unfortunately was killed.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.830
And it was so shocking and traumatic,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.785
as anything would be like that.

00:02:30.785 --> 00:02:34.417
And, I naturally, my human instinct was,

00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:36.660
"Okay, I'm just gonna
leave this for a while.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.600
People will understand why
I'm not continuing to write."

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.433
- Yeah.
- I go,

00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:41.266
"How am I gonna put a book out

00:02:41.266 --> 00:02:43.470
on "Grits, Grace, and Gratitude,"
and my mom just died?"

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.011
- Yeah.

00:02:45.011 --> 00:02:47.250
- And then, somebody on my
team said, "But, wait a minute.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.020
You know, let's think about it.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.450
Jackie could be throughout this book.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.740
And, her last text to me
was, "Think you'll be happy."

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.877
Those are the last
words my mom said to me,

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.820
"Think you'll be happy."

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.360
And, we just moved it
all together, and went,

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.040
"Wait a minute, that's
the title of the book,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.310
because it is the mantra that she gave me.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.630
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- To live my life.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.780
- It's amazing to me to think
about everything changed.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.610
And, I'm a person that
thinks everything happens

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.237
for a reason, even if it's horrible.

00:03:16.237 --> 00:03:17.070
- Me too.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.810
- And, it's one of
those things, it's like,

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.920
how in incredibly magical
that they still live on

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.629
through this book that you were writing,

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:24.142
that was supposedly about something else,

00:03:24.142 --> 00:03:26.130
and now it becomes
something bigger than that.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.810
And, so much more helpful, by the way,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.754
to all the people that are
going through such grief

00:03:29.754 --> 00:03:30.728
and loss.
- I agree.

00:03:30.728 --> 00:03:32.274
- Yeah.
- And, 'cause grief comes

00:03:32.274 --> 00:03:34.440
in different waves, as we all know.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.300
- Oh, I think divorce is grief.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.100
That's a death.
- It's grief. It's a death.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.040
- Yeah.
- And relationships die.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.168
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And, dogs die.

00:03:41.168 --> 00:03:42.334
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.980
- And, parents die, and
children, or no one has to die.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.860
Grief is, you could lose a
job that you love so much.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.693
- Yeah.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.022
- And all of a sudden you're
fired. You lose something.

00:03:50.022 --> 00:03:52.235
But, like I say in the
book, it is the receipt,

00:03:52.235 --> 00:03:56.520
grief is the receipt that you loved,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.420
that you loved something.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.680
'Cause if you didn't, you wouldn't.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.239
- This is why I told her to write a book!

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.072
(all laugh)
(audience cheers)

00:04:01.072 --> 00:04:02.930
It's a bumper sticker. I'm like, what?

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:06.132
I would wear that on
a shirt as a reminder.

00:04:06.132 --> 00:04:08.910
- It is a receipt that you've loved,

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.200
and you've been loved, hopefully.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.033
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:11.966 --> 00:04:14.100
- And, that's really what
this journey of life is.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.660
All of us are gonna feel grief.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.660
All of us are gonna feel sadness.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.956
- To know that it's inevitable.

00:04:19.956 --> 00:04:20.789
- It's inevitable.

00:04:20.789 --> 00:04:23.670
Trials and tribulations come to everybody.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:24.503
- Yeah.

00:04:24.503 --> 00:04:27.030
- And so, I was hoping
that this book, kind of,

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.016
yes, it's about moving
through grief, of course,

00:04:29.016 --> 00:04:31.191
but it also is about living,
this book is about life.

00:04:31.191 --> 00:04:32.024
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:32.024 --> 00:04:36.300
- This book is about survival,
and legacy, and love,

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.990
and compassion, and
serving others, you know,

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.460
and I just used my Mom.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.390
- Which makes me feel
so great serving others.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:45.016
- Yeah, so I use, I was able
to take the pain that I felt

00:04:45.016 --> 00:04:47.430
for what happened to my mom.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.790
And, I thought, "Well the
best way I can honor her

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.840
is to live a full life, and
do things that made her happy

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.640
so that it continues her legacy."

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.120
- And, then make you happy.
- And talk about her.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.100
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.620
And, I never wanted anyone
to forget Jacqueline Avant.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.730
And, I thought, "You know what?

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.250
If there's all this news about my mom,

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:10.230
and it's so sensational, then
I'm gonna write her story."

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:11.063
- Yeah.

00:05:11.063 --> 00:05:12.390
- "I'm gonna talk about Jacqueline Avant.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.680
- But, who would know it best?

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.882
- Right.
- Yeah.

00:05:14.882 --> 00:05:15.715
- You know, so.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.548
- It's a beautiful book,

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:18.069
and it's.
- Thank you.

00:05:18.069 --> 00:05:19.170
- It's gonna be helpful to so many,

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.300
it's a lot of hardship
you had to go through,

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.040
but it's a beautiful thing
to be able to use that,

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.873
your testimony.

00:05:23.873 --> 00:05:24.706
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:05:24.706 --> 00:05:25.715
- Thank you.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:25.715 --> 00:05:26.580
- Thank you.
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.517
- Yes.
- Nicole's book,

00:05:27.517 --> 00:05:29.370
"Think You'll Be Happy," is out now.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.053
Y'all gotta get yourself a copy.

